  "notes": "{通|とお}す is a versatile transitive verb with three main meanings: letting something pass through, persisting to completion, and showing someone in.\n\nTRANSITIVITY:\n- Type: ⟦{他動詞|たどうし}→他動詞：10418_tadoushi⟧ (transitive)\n- Pair: ⟦{通|とお}る→通る：01243_tooru⟧ (intransitive, to pass through)\n\nCOMMON PATTERNS:\n- ⟦{光|ひかり}→光：01707_hikari⟧⟦を→を：00422_wo⟧{通|とお}す: to let light through\n- ⟦{針|はり}→針：03566_hari⟧⟦に→に：00314_ni⟧⟦{糸|いと}→糸：01315_ito⟧⟦を→を：00422_wo⟧{通|とお}す: to thread a needle\n- ⟦{意見|いけん}→意見：01303_iken⟧⟦を→を：00422_wo⟧{通|とお}す: to get one's opinion accepted\n- ⟦{筋|すじ}→筋：03366_suji⟧⟦を→を：00422_wo⟧{通|とお}す: to be consistent\n- ⟦お{客|きゃく}さん→お客さん：10253_okyakusan⟧⟦を→を：00422_wo⟧{通|とお}す: to show a guest in\n\nAS SUFFIX (-{通|とお}す):\nAttaches to verb stems to mean 'do through to completion':\n- ⟦{読|よ}み→読む：00426_yomu⟧{通|とお}す: to read through entirely\n- ⟦やり→やる：02980_yaru⟧{通|とお}す: to see through to the end",
